"help.faq.content" = "Q: Unable to connect?\nA: Make sure both devices are on the same Wi-Fi network and USB Debugging is enabled.\n\nQ: Connection keeps dropping?\nA: Check Wi-Fi stability or restart Wireless Debugging.\n\nQ: Can’t find Developer Options?\nA: Open Settings → About and tap the build number seven times.\n\nQ: A command failed?\nA: Check the device connection. Some commands require root access.";
"help.faq.title" = "FAQ";
"help.features.content" = "• App Manager: install, uninstall, clear data, and force stop\n• File Manager: browse, upload, download, and delete device files\n• TV Remote: control smart TVs and streaming boxes\n• Command Center: quickly run common device commands\n• Shell Terminal: run custom commands\n• Device Info: view detailed system and hardware information";
"help.quick.start.content" = "1. Connect the Android device and iPhone to the same Wi-Fi network\n2. Enable Developer Options and USB Debugging on the Android device\n3. Tap “Connect Device” on the Home screen\n4. Choose a connection method and enter the device details\n5. Once connected, all features are ready to use";
"help.quick.start.title" = "Quick Start";
"help.security.content" = "• Use only on trusted Wi-Fi networks\n• Turn off Wireless Debugging when not in use\n• Do not enable device debugging in public places\n• Review the connected-device list regularly\n• Be cautious with commands from unfamiliar sources";
"help.security.title" = "Security Tips";
"help.subtitle" = "Quick Start Guide";
"help.wifi.content" = "For all Android versions:\n\n1. Enable network debugging for the device on a computer (default port 5555)\n2. Find the IP address under Settings → About → Status on the Android device\n3. Enter the IP address and port 5555 in Scarab\n4. Tap Connect\n\nNote: The first connection requires setup on a computer. Later connections can be made directly.";
"help.wireless.content" = "For Android 11 or later:\n\n1. Open Settings → Developer Options → Wireless Debugging\n2. Enable Wireless Debugging\n3. Tap “Pair device with pairing code”\n4. Enter the displayed IP address, port, and pairing code in Scarab\n5. Connect after pairing completes\n\nBenefit: Pair directly without a computer.";
